# ==============================================================================
# .gitignore — Real-Time Sign Language to Text Conversion System
# ==============================================================================
# Guiding rule (docs/RULES.md §Git): commit CODE, CONFIG, DOCS and small
# EVIDENCE artifacts. Never commit datasets, model binaries, secrets, or
# anything containing a person's likeness.
# ==============================================================================

# --- Python --------------------------------------------------------------------
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*$py.class
*.so
.Python
build/
develop-eggs/
dist/
downloads/
eggs/
.eggs/
lib64/
parts/
sdist/
var/
wheels/
*.egg-info/
.installed.cfg
*.egg
MANIFEST

# --- Virtual environments ------------------------------------------------------
.venv/
venv/
env/
ENV/
.python-version

# --- Secrets & local overrides -------------------------------------------------
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
config.local.yaml
secrets.yaml
*.pem
*.key

# ==============================================================================
# DATASET — never committed
# ==============================================================================
# Two reasons, both important:
#   1. SIZE: thousands of .npz/.jpg files bloat the repo and every clone.
#   2. PRIVACY: this data is derived from webcam recordings of real people
#      (our own team). Pushing it to a hosted remote publishes their likeness.
#      See docs/RULES.md §Privacy.
#
# What IS committed instead: the metadata that makes the dataset reproducible —
# the class registry and session manifests (small JSON/CSV, no imagery).
# ==============================================================================
data/raw/**
data/interim/**
data/processed/**
data/features/**

# Keep the directory skeleton so a fresh clone has somewhere to write
!data/**/.gitkeep

# DO commit dataset metadata — it documents methodology without shipping data
!data/metadata/
!data/metadata/**
data/metadata/**/*.npz
data/metadata/**/*.npy

# Explicit media/array excludes anywhere under data/
*.npz
*.npy
*.jpg
*.jpeg
*.png
*.mp4
*.avi
*.mov
!docs/assets/**
!reports/figures/**

# ==============================================================================
# MODELS — binaries not committed
# ==============================================================================
# A trained .joblib is a build output, not source. It is regenerated by
# `python scripts/train_model.py`. Committing binaries makes diffs meaningless
# and the repo grows with every retrain.
#
# EXCEPTION: model_metadata.json IS committed. It is small, human-readable, and
# is the audit trail of what was trained, when, on which feature set, with what
# scores. That is the evidence a grader actually wants to see.
# ==============================================================================
models/**/*.joblib
models/**/*.pkl
models/**/*.h5
models/**/*.onnx
!models/**/model_metadata.json
!models/**/.gitkeep

# ==============================================================================
# REPORTS & LOGS
# ==============================================================================
# Evaluation figures and metrics ARE committed — they are the project's evidence
# for the 80-mark submission and must be reviewable in the repo history.
logs/*.log
logs/*.log.*
!logs/.gitkeep

# --- Notebook checkpoints ------------------------------------------------------
.ipynb_checkpoints/
notebooks/**/*.nbconvert.ipynb

# --- Testing & tooling caches --------------------------------------------------
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
.coverage.*
htmlcov/
coverage.xml
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.tox/
.hypothesis/

# --- Editors & IDEs ------------------------------------------------------------
.vscode/
!.vscode/settings.json.example
.idea/
*.swp
*.swo
*~

# --- OS artifacts --------------------------------------------------------------
# This repo lives inside a OneDrive-synced folder, so Windows/OneDrive droppings
# are especially likely to appear.
Thumbs.db
ehthumbs.db
Desktop.ini
desktop.ini
$RECYCLE.BIN/
*.lnk
.DS_Store
.AppleDouble

# --- Temporary files -----------------------------------------------------------
tmp/
temp/
*.tmp
*.bak
*.orig
